{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/bin/fake_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T23:26:33.546710Z","id":"f322a56049a3f963295365e16072524115cf8deb3d2712053c2eb08f3664eb39","body":{"detail":"Observed against a real `clax serve` (bazel-bin/crates/clax-cli/clax) on a scratch home: a fake_host process serving when the daemon is stopped by SIGTERM and started again on the same home and port exits 1 with 'fake_host: serve: 0 {\"error\":{\"code\":\"transport\",...}}', because every Served::Refused other than 404 ends the loop (line 85). A new fake_host process cannot take over either: the CLI takes no registration ID, so FakeHost::resume is unreachable from it and it registers afresh, and calls waiting for the old registration are never delivered to it. A real-process restart check of docs/contract.md 'Going on as a registration' therefore needs a host written outside fake_host (raw HTTP). Either a --registration <id> flag (FakeHost::resume) with --registered-file to write the ID, or retrying status 0 with a bounded backoff, would let fake_host cover it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":63},"end":{"line":87},"content_hash":"448582bbe93613559e684a766dd507568618f513827e61a71dd7ee54dc259c0c"},"summary":"fake_host cannot serve across a daemon restart: it exits on a refused connection and has no flag to go on as a registration ID","tags":["testkit","claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-testkit/src/bin/fake_host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:58:30.681040Z","id":"5f413418b39f46281cc0025986a2ab832ededcdc1667cae2d3ecbb33f8a25a72","body":{"detail":"Commit 2372cfe6a (crates/clax-testkit/src/bin/fake_host.rs): --registration <id> goes on as that ID; --registration-file <path> is read when it exists and written each time the host registers; an ID the daemon does not know is registered afresh and said on stderr. A transport failure (status 0) or a 401 unauthorized (a restarted daemon has a new token) is tried again after a pause growing from 100 ms to 5 s, with --token-file read again (it may be a home's daemon.json), until --retry-for seconds of pauses (default 0 keeps the old exit 1). Unit tests in crates/clax-testkit/src/bin/fake_host/tests.rs (//crates/clax-testkit:fake_host_bin_test, 12 pass). Commit 11a336c4a: scripts/smoke-bot-surfaces.sh (just smoke-bot-surfaces) restarts a real clax serve on the same home and port while a run is parked on desk.ask; a fake_host started while the daemon was down, with the same registration file, went on as the registration, was sent the waiting question (same id and key), and the run finished; each of the four keys applied once. Run on 2026-11-11: all PASS lines, exit 0. Not done: a fake_host kept running across the restart is covered only by the retry unit tests, not by the smoke (its host-2 is stopped before the restart because it never answers the question).","kind":"comment","references":"f322a56049a3f963295365e16072524115cf8deb3d2712053c2eb08f3664eb39","summary":"fake_host now takes --registration, --registration-file and --retry-for; scripts/smoke-bot-surfaces.sh covers the real-process restart","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
